  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Since 1953, the Brun family has run this seafood brasserie at 27 rue (cours) Félix Faure, at the corner of rue Louis Blanc, steps from the harbour and the Palais des Festivals. Seafood platters, oysters, mussels, fish soup, sole meunière: a lively brasserie atmosphere. Cannes Tourisme describes terraces with views of Le Suquet and the place des Allées.</p>

      <h2>Dogs at the table</h2>
      <p>The Cannes Tourisme (tourist office) listing says "Animals accepted" among the amenities. It gives a capacity of 70 seats, all on the terrace, plus 3 air-conditioned rooms, but does not say whether dogs are admitted indoors or only on the terrace. The restaurant's official website does not mention animals.</p>
      <p>The restaurant takes no reservations, and the official website notes that last orders are at 9:30pm. Seafood is served every day non-stop from 12pm to 9:30pm; menu dishes are served 12pm-2pm and 7pm-9:30pm on weekdays, non-stop 12pm-9:30pm at weekends. Expect €30 to €70 à la carte according to Cannes Tourisme.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> where the dog may sit (terrace or room), to ask on arrival. Beware of opening hours found elsewhere: the restaurant's former domain name has been taken over by a third party; only astouxetbrun.fr is reliable.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: no reservations — I arrive outside peak hours and ask at the front desk whether I can stay on the terrace with my human.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is steps from Le Suquet and the harbour of Cannes: a stroll through the lanes of the old quarter extends the meal.</p>
      <p><small>Sources read on 06/11/2026: official website astouxetbrun.fr, Cannes Tourisme listing (cannes-france.com).</small></p>
